<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · South Asia</p><h1 class="st-title">Polonnaruwa Kingdom</h1><p class="st-meta">1070 CE – 1232 CE (approx.) · capital Polonnaruwa</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The second great Sinhalese kingdom, which drove out the Cholas and under Parakramabahu I built the Parakrama Samudra and the Gal Vihara.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>After the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/chola-empire">Chola Empire</a> conquered the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/anuradhapura-kingdom">Anuradhapura Kingdom</a> in the early 11th century, it ruled northern <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/sri-lanka">Sri Lanka</a> from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/polonnaruwa">Polonnaruwa</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vijayabahu-i">Vijayabahu I</a>, leading resistance from the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-ruhuna">Kingdom of Ruhuna</a>, expelled the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chola-empire">Cholas</a> in 1070 and kept Polonnaruwa as his capital.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/parakramabahu-i">Parakramabahu I</a>, who ruled from 1153 to 1186, reunited the island after a civil war, built the vast reservoir called the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/parakrama-samudra">Parakrama Samudra</a>, reformed and unified the Buddhist sangha and sent expeditions to <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/myanmar">Burma</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-india">South India</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/polonnaruwa">Polonnaruwa's</a> palaces, image houses and the rock-cut Buddhas of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gal-vihara">Gal Vihara</a> date from this time. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nissanka-malla">Nissanka Malla</a>, from <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-kalinga">Kalinga</a>, left many inscriptions. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rice">Rice</a> grown with irrigation and trade sustained the kingdom.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>After <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nissanka-malla">Nissanka Malla</a> the kingdom was torn by rivalries. In 1215 the invader <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kalinga-magha">Kalinga Magha</a> sacked <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/polonnaruwa">Polonnaruwa</a>, and around 1232 the Sinhalese capital moved south-west to <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-dambadeniya">Dambadeniya</a>. The irrigation network of the dry zone fell into decay.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/polonnaruwa-kingdom.jpg" alt="Polonnaruwa Kingdom" width="320" height="446"><figcaption>Image: Yixopeh377 · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Anuradhapura_Kingdom_Infinity_Resolution.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1070 CE – 1232 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/11th-century">11th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>bureaucratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Polonnaruwa</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Vijayabahu I, Parakramabahu I, Nissanka Malla</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Theravada Buddhism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Sinhala, Pali</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/sri-lanka">Sri Lanka</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Kingdom of Polonnaruwa</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1151&amp;focus=polonnaruwa-kingdom" aria-label="Polonnaruwa Kingdom on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="6920 1881 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Polonnaruwa Kingdom lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M7240 2137L7224 2158M7240 2137L7222 2122M7240 2137L7208 2073M7240 2137L7218 2158"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M7224 2158h0M7222 2122h0M7208 2073h0M7218 2158h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M7240 2137h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M7240 2137h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Polonnaruwa. <a href="/atlas?year=1151&amp;focus=polonnaruwa-kingdom">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
